{
 "brief": "Rajaa Abu Moussa, 27, has lived in a tent for more than two and a half years after an airstrike on her family home in al-Nuseirat camp, central Gaza, left her paralyzed from the waist down, Shehab Wire reported. The damage to her lower body rendered her unable to move independently, forcing her into displacement within her own territory.\n\nAbu Moussa's case illustrates the long-term human toll beyond casualty counts, as survivors across Gaza contend with severe injuries, displacement, and inadequate living conditions in makeshift shelters.",
